class_name CryptEnemyData
extends RefCounted
## Level 2 — The Catacombs — enemy definitions (Minifantasy_Undead_Creatures pack).
##
## Twelve rank-and-file roles; the miniboss and final boss live in their own factories
## (SkeletonMinotaurData / ZombieGiantData) because bosses carry choreographed skills.
##
##   crypt_fodder        Headless Skeleton          — fragile melee swarm
##   crypt_swarmer       Jumping Skull              — fastest unit, paper-thin
##   crypt_skirmisher    Reanimated Skeleton Warrior— standard melee
##   crypt_raider        Reanimated Zombie Warrior  — slower, meatier melee
##   crypt_archer        Reanimated Skeleton Archer — ranged, arrow
##   crypt_zombie_archer Reanimated Zombie Archer   — tougher ranged, heavier arrow
##   crypt_caster        Reanimated Skeleton Mage   — ranged, spell bolt
##   crypt_zombie_caster Reanimated Zombie Mage     — tougher caster, curse bolt
##   crypt_ghost         Ghost                      — fast harasser, ignores armour
##   crypt_brute         Zombie Bear                — heavy
##   crypt_heavy         Zombie Minotaur            — heaviest rank-and-file
##   crypt_cavalry       Skeletal Horse + Rider     — fast charger
##
## Scenes are generated by tools/gen_undead_scenes.gd. Registered in EnemyRegistry.
##
## Scaling intent: The Catacombs is biome 2, so the line troops sit roughly 1.5-2x the
## equivalent cave role. Cave reference: fodder 8hp/6dmg, swarmer 12/6, brute 90/20/8armor.

